\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  COLUMN-Turkish inflation fight may need lira boost\b0\par\par\uc2 753 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2011\par 12:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 -- Neal Kimberley is an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst for Reuters. The opinions expressed are his own --\par \par \uc2 By Neal Kimberley\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 14 (Reuters) - The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy mix, with its attendant objective of weakening the lira <TRY=>, might need some tweaking as the fight against inflation may be set to hot up.\par \par \uc2 With this in mind, traders might feel the rally in USD/TRY to Monday's 1.5800 from a November low of 1.3830 has run its course.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers around the world have been turning their fire on inflation [ID:nLDE7091HX], but the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has adopted an unorthodox monetary policy combining rises in reserve requirements with benchmark interest rate cuts. [ID:nLDE70Q0L5]\par \par \uc2 Ankara's objective has been to make yields less attractive, lessening international investor demand for the lira and aiding Turkish exporters' competitiveness, while simultaneously raising reserve requirements to drain excess liquidity and curb credit growth. [ID:nLDE70O0VF]\par \par \uc2 If lira weakening is a measure of this policy's success, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably be satisfied, but addressing inflation worries may require a different policy tool kit.\par \par \uc2 A weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no help when seeking to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 25, the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its mid-point inflation forecast from 5.4 percent to 5.9 percent, citing concern over higher fuel prices, but predicting its current policy mix would remain in place for a long time.\par \par \uc2 Maybe. But in a Reuters poll of 15 banks, 10 expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its benchmark one-week repo rate on hold at 6.25 percent when it makes its rate decision on Feb. 15 [ID:nLDE71910N]\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 25, Brent crude <LC0c1> was trading at $95 a barrel compared to $101 on Monday, which may test even Finance Minister Mehmet Simsek's confidence that Turkey's economy is strong enough to handle current oil prices. [ID:nLDE719075]\par \par \uc2 Moreover, while Turkey's consumer price inflation slowed to 4.9 percent on an annualised basis, from 6.4 percent in December and well inside the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's year-end target of 5.5 percent, the producer price index is on the rise.\par \par \uc2 Producer prices rose 2.36 percent on the month, exceeding a forecast rise of 1.0 percent, to give an annual increase of 10.8 percent and fanning fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent benchmark rate cuts may leave \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  unprepared for any later inflation spike. [ID:nLDE7120H1]\par \par \uc2 State \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower meat prices is already evident with the government having authorised meat imports -- much to the chagrin of domestic producers. [ID:nLDE70B04A]\par \par \uc2 While ratings agencies Fitch and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  are supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unorthodox policy mix [ID:nLDE71809N], traders might feel a further slide in the lira is inconsistent with controlling price pressures.\par \par \uc2 STRONG RECOVERY\par \par \uc2 It is not as if Turkey's economy clearly needs a further boost from a weaker lira.\par \par \uc2 Simsek said on Thursday that economic recovery was strong and that while growth would not be at the pace of 8-9 percent per annum, he expected around 5 percent in 2011. [ID:nLDE71909I]\par \par \uc2 Data released on Tuesday showed industrial output rose 16.9 percent year-on-year in December, far exceeding a Reuters poll forecast for a rise of 11 percent. [ID:nIST007569]\par \par \uc2 Of course it is undeniable that the current account deficit, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new monetary policy was largely designed to address, is worsening.\par \par \uc2 The deficit surged 132 percent to a record high of $7.529 billion in December, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Friday, exceeding the median forecast of $7.0 billion in a Reuters poll of 14 analysts. [ID:nLDE71A0H9]\par \par \uc2 Be that as it may, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Durmus Yilmaz [ID:nLDE716235], in a Feb. 7 interview with Reuters and Reuters Insider, highlighted the potentially inflationary impact of further lira weakening.\par \par \uc2 "We are very mindful that any further ... depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if commodity prices increase further, will impact the inflation outlook in a negative way," Yilmaz said.\par \par \uc2 Given that Yilmaz also argued that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to cool inflows of speculative capital seem to be succeeding, perhaps his attention might turn more to inflationary concerns.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest in weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further might abate, leaving the field open to the lira bulls.\par \par \uc2 Biography of author [ID:nL9197090]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY (\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  COLUMN)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110214e72e0011m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
