\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish lira weakens, inflation data eyed   \b0\par\par\uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2007\par 07:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Dec 3 (Reuters) - Turkey's lira weakened on Monday as Asian stocks fell and investors awaited guidance from Turkish inflation data due later in the day.   \par \par \uc2  Traders shrugged off news at the weekend from the Turkish armed forces that they had inflicted heavy casualties on Kurdish separatist militants in a "intense \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " into northern Iraq.   \par \par \uc2  The army said \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue and President Abdullah Gul reaffirmed on Sunday \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's readiness and right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in northern Iraq.   \par \par \uc2  Investors said limited \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  against separatist Kurdish guerrillas had been expected. On Friday, the lira had weakened slightly after Prime Minister Tayyip Erdogan said the government had authorised the army to carry out an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  into northern Iraq.   \par \par \uc2  The lira <IYIX=> weakened to 1.1830 in early interbank trade, from an official close of 1.1770 on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  "I expect the market to be quiet today until inflation," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2  "If inflation comes in between 1.5 and 2.0 percent, that is priced in, if it comes in above or below that the market will react," he said, adding that because of a series of holidays in December, investors are already starting to close their books for year-end and position themselves for 2008.   \par \par \uc2  Inflation data is due at 1500 GMT on Monday. A forecast from a Reuters poll put the monthly consumer inflation rate at 1.46 percent after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned prices could spike higher in November before returning to a downward trend.   \par \par \uc2  Consumer price inflation in Istanbul came in at 1.94 percent in November, the Istanbul Chamber of Commerce said on Monday.   \par \par \uc2  Asian stocks weakened on Monday and then yen, which is closely watched by lira investors, firmed in a sign of lower risk appetite. Investors borrow the cheap Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest in high-yielding lira, helping the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate almost 20 percent this year.   \par \par \uc2  After the market closed on Friday data showed Turkey's trade deficit widened 30.7 percent year-on-year to $5.633 billion in October, just below a Reuters poll forecast of $5.925 billion.   \par \par \uc2  On Saturday data from the Turkish Exporters Association showed that in November exports surged 29 percent year-on-year to $11.11 billion.   \par \par \uc2  Stocks in focus on Monday will include conglomerates  \uc2 Koc Holding\uc2   and  \uc2 Sabanci Holding\uc2  , which posted nine-month results after the market closed on Friday. On Monday Koc's chairman was also quoted as saying revenue would come in at $45 billion this year, rising to $50 billion in 2008.   \par \par \uc2  Media group Dogan Yayin , its parent Dogan Holding , and  \uc2 Turkish Airlines\uc2   also published profit figures.   \par \par \uc2  On Friday the main stock index <.XU100> rose 1.94 percent to 54,213.82 points. The yield on the Aug. 5, 2009 benchmark bond <0#TRTSYSUM=IS> fell to 16.63 percent from Thursday's close of 16.66 percent.  (Reporting by Irem Koker)     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY/PREOPENER|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071203e3c3000gd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
