\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Turkish cbank dollar auction 7 times overbid   \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2007\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details background, comment)   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, July 25 (Reuters) - Bids at Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily dollar-buying auction were $288 million, more than seven times a maximum buying limit of $40 million, data showed on Wednesday at the first auction since it raised the buying limit.   \par \par \uc2 The bank bought $40 million, the full amount, at a maximum price of 1.2475 lira <IYIX=>, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.   \par \par \uc2 Raymond James Chief Economist Ozgur Altug said bid volume was the second highest since 2002.   \par \par \uc2 "This shows that there is plenty of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply, which will exert pressure on the exchange rate in the coming period. If this trend continues, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The bank said on Tuesday dollar supply growth was likely to top dollar demand in the coming period and it was increasing the maximum amount of dollars it would buy at its daily auctions to $40 million from a previous $15 million.   \par \par \uc2 It also increased the maximum amount it would buy in an option facility after the auction to $80 million from $30 million. The option price is the price established at the tender.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought the maximum $80 million in option sales after Wednesday's auction.   \par \par \uc2 Dollar selling by locals who had increased their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings in the run-up to Sunday's general election is underpinning the lira, while foreigners reassured by the pro-business AK Party's win are buying the high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 TURKEY-CBANK/AUCTION (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070725e37p001fq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
