\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Mkt Debt Struggles; Political Tension Hits Turkey   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Wailin Wong   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2007\par 22:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market bonds had a hard time keeping afloat Monday, with the asset class falling far behind a rally in U.S. Treasurys.   \par \par \uc2 Spreads on  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus were seven basis points wider at 164 basis points over Treasurys, which gained on tame March inflation data. On Friday, the EMBI+ had closed at 157 basis points, matching a record-tight level set earlier this month.   \par \par \uc2 One New York-based debt trader said volumes were quiet ahead of Tuesday's May Day holiday, which will shut every major Latin American market, as well as other countries in Asia and Europe.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging markets showed signs of fatigue last week, with many credits at record-tight spreads but little momentum for further gains.  \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  said in a Monday report that valuations on emerging market debt "appear increasingly uncompelling."   \par \par \uc2 Turkey grabbed headlines Monday as political tension gripped the country. Hundreds of thousands of anti-government demonstrators took the streets in Istanbul Sunday to demand the resignation of the AK Party government. Late Friday, the military issued a statement saying it might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ward off what it described as threats to \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's secular institutions. The AKP's presidential candidate, Foreign Minister Abdullah Gul, failed to win the office in voting last week. A second round is scheduled for May 2.   \par \par \uc2 Turkey's Global 2030 bond tumbled 1 9/16 to 154 5/8 bid, according to Reuters, and its EMBI+ spread mushroomed 16 basis points to 210 basis points over Treasurys. Its five-year credit default swaps were 20 basis points wider at 165 basis points mid-level late in the European session, and the New York-based trader said the CDS were little traded during U.S. hours.   \par \par \uc2 Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened in line with Turkish assets, but external debt from the region performed slightly better. Poland's EMBI+ spread tightened two basis points to 48 basis points over Treasurys.   \par \par \uc2 Mexico's Global 2034 rose 3/4 to 111 1/2 bid and its EMBI+ spread widened two basis points to 88 basis points over Treasurys. The credit posted positive returns on the day despite the Bank of Mexico lowering its 2007 forecast for the country's growth to between 3% and 3.5%, compared with a previous projection of 3.25% to 3.75%. Finance Minister Agustin Carstens said in Canada earlier Monday that the ministry will likely revise downward its growth projection to 3.3% from 3.6%.   \par \par \uc2 Colombia's Global 2033 jumped 1 3/8 to 148 5/8 bid and its EMBI+ spread widened five basis points to 139 basis points over Treasurys. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its monthly monetary policy meeting Monday and is expected to raise the benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points to 8.5%. UBS said policymakers "will have to maintain a hawkish stance" to bring inflation back within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 3.5% to 4.5%.   \par \par \uc2 -By Wailin Wong, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 5240; wailin.wong@dowjones.com [ 30-04-07 2014GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1179 1810 4071   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070430e34u001cs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
