\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging debt-Turkey's bonds move to the beat set by the lira  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases  \par \uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2006\par 14:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, June 26 (Reuters) - Turkey's sovereign dollar-donominated bonds fell sharply on Monday in thin trading as investors trimmed positions while weighing the impact of more rate increases and dollar sales by Ankara.  \par \par \uc2 "If there is stability on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  side things it will get better on the external side. Bond traders are looking at the lira and more action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey will be welcomed by the market," said Luis Costa, emerging markets strategist at ING in London.  \par \par \uc2 On Sunday Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates 225 basis points. On Monday it followed through on promises to sell dollars at auction, conducted direct dollar selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as draining more lira liquidity from the system with "depo" auctions.  \par \par \uc2 Trading in the lira was a tug of war on Monday, with initial strength giving way to selling only to be bolstered again with the dollar auction and direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark sovereign dollar bond due 2030 <TRGLB30=> was down on the day, clearly the underperformer for the emerging debt sector as a whole, but strength in the lira has helped cut early losses.  \par \par \uc2 The 2030 bond is down 1.188 points in price to bid 132.375, yielding 8.636 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark JP Morgan Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus (EMBI+) <11EMJ> <.JPMEMBIPLUS> however showed the sector was holding up much better with yield spreads wider by just one basis point to 229 basis points over U.S. Treasuries.  \par \par \uc2 Turkey's EMBI+ portion showed yield spreads wider by 16 basis points to 252 over Treasuries.  \par \par \uc2 "Invstors still trying to unload their neutral and overweighted positions on Turkey, which I think will continue over the next weeks. Unfortunately this is not going to fade away over a number of days," Costa cautioned.  \par \par \uc2 Given the low liquidity in the market, investors have turned to the credit default swaps market to unload their risk. The CDS market offers sovereign debt holders protection against default or restructuring. Widening spreads show increased risk aversion.  \par \par \uc2 Turkey's five-year CDS <TURKEY5UA=GFI> spread has pushed the bid price up to 320 basis points, its highest level in over a year and up from 115 basis points in February.  \par \par \uc2 "The trading in the market overall has been illiquid and erratic. Turkey especially and that's pushing people into CDS. There is still no conviction (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is going to get it right," said one senior trader at a German bank in London.  \par \par \uc2 LIMITED MOVES  \par \par \uc2 The deterioration in Turkish CDS is now on par with five-year CDS from Argentina and Ecuador and worse than Peru and Jamaica. Elsewhere, Brazil's 2040 bond, the most liquid emerging sovereign debt issue, traded up 0.25 points in price to bid 121.938, yielding 7.619 percent <BRAGLB40=RR>.  \par \par \uc2 Russia's 2030 bond <RUSGLB30=RR> fell 0.438 points in price to bid 105.250, yielding 6.541 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, dollar-denominated bonds in Russian steelmaker Severstal plunged on news its bid to buy Luxembourg-based Arcelor failed against a higher offer from Mittal Steel that values Arcelor, according to a Reuters calculation, at roughly 25.6 billion euros.  \par \par \uc2 Severstal's 2014 bond <RU019049060=> was bid down 3.65 points in price to 103.78, pushing the yield up to 8.572 percent. Spreads over the benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury widened by 62 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 Russian politicians slammed Arcelor's deicision, saying it showed an anti-Russian bias in international markets.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING-DEBT|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060629e26q0010c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
