\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sells dollars to steady lira  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Asli Kandemir  \par \uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2006\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds bond yield, quote)  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, June 23 (Reuters) - The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, selling dollars after the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to a March 2003 low of 1.71/dollar.  \par \par \uc2 It was the second bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in less than two weeks and prompted a short-lived rebound in the lira. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  then fell back to trade at 1.7000 at 1040 GMT, 0.2 percent weaker on the day.  \par \par \uc2 It was still more than 20 percent weaker than its level at the end of April. Since then investors have been spooked by sharply higher than expected inflation, political tensions and a flight of funds from emerging markets generally.  \par \par \uc2 "It was observed that the excessive fluctuations in the exchange rate have continued in recent days, linked to a liquidity squeeze," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 The size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not immediately clear. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has $58.3 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 "The 1.70 level is creating tension in the market, but I think it will test above this level to see how aggressive the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on the secondary bond market followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the April 9, 2008 benchmark <0#TRTSYSUM=IS> yield climbing to 21.01 percent, the highest level seen since December 2004.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is a bit nervous and buyers are just following the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. We have basic fundamental concerns about inflation and further inflation because of rapid devaluation of the lira," one banker said.  \par \par \uc2 The lira briefly strengthened on Thursday on news of tax cuts for investors, but gave up those gains amid global weakness in emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market selling dollars on June 13 after a sharp hike in interest rates failed to halt the lira's slide.  \par \par \uc2 That was its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the lira since May 2004 and amounted to some $700 million.  \par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATE SPECULATION  \par \par \uc2 The bank made a surprise 175 basis point hike in overnight interest rates earlier this month amid concerns that Turkey will far overshoot its end-2006 inflation target of 5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Economists are keenly awaiting the June inflation data on July 3 and will be looking out for the possibility of further rate hikes in the coming months.  \par \par \uc2 "I do not think the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be enough to calm the markets. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to raise interest rates by at least 100 basis points in July. But the real problem is that confidence in the government has been undermined," said one economist, who declined to be named.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left key interest rates unchanged this week and said they were more likely to remain stable than go up, but it said it was prepared to tighten monetary policy to rein in inflation.  \par \par \uc2 The main share index <.XU100> ended the morning session down 1.35 percent at 33,767 points.  \par \par \uc2 Political tensions centre on the possibility of early general elections, tensions between the Islamist-rooted ruling party and secularists and concerns that the Cyprus problem will obstruct Turkey's progress towards European Union membership.  \par \par \uc2 Ankara is under pressure to move towards recognition of EU member state Cyprus's internationally accepted Greek Cypriot government. It currently backs breakaway Turkish Cypriots.  \par \par \uc2 Investors have fled emerging markets generally as higher U.S. rates attract funds and monetary tightening at the Bank of Japan reduces a source of cheap cash.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Thomas Grove)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 TURKEY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060623e26n000hp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
