\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish assets seen weak ahead of cbank meeting  \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2006\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, June 6 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira retreated in early trade against the dollar on Tuesday amid continued worries over inflation ahead of Wednesday's meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee which seems set to hike rates.  \par \par \uc2 Overnight falls in global markets will also cloud investors' mood as they await the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision, bankers said.  \par \par \uc2 The lira <IYIX=> traded at around 1.5820 to the dollar at 0607 GMT, down from its Monday close of 1.5750. The lira briefly hit a three-year low of 1.6220 to the greenback late last Friday after May data showing a spike in inflation data was published.  \par \par \uc2 The data showed prices rose more than twice as fast as expected during May, eroding the purchasing power of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pushing up the price of borrowing.  \par \par \uc2 "People are waiting to see what happens at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee tomorrow. What will be important are the extent of the rate rise and the signals given to the markets," said one banker.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on the benchmark April 9, 2008 bond <0#TRTSYSUM=IS> traded as high as 18.9 percent on Monday, the highest since February 2005.  \par \par \uc2 The main Istanbul stock index <.XU100> fell 3.36 percent to 37,964.03 points on Monday, also knocked by the inflation figures, and brokers said they expected more falls on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect selling today. Global markets are negative... We do not think the market volatility has ended yet," said Ali Ria Incekara of Raymond James Research.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting is positive, but we think a rate rise of 50 basis points or less will not be enough to calm the volatility," he added.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of 22 economists gave a median forecast of a 50 point rise, although forecasts varied widely.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Durmus Yilmaz has been quoted in local media as saying he is personally in favour of raising interest rates and that the bank could use its $60 billion reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 TURKEY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -PREOPENER|LANGEN|ABN|M|MD|D|E|RBN|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060606e266000mk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
