\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  in no hurry to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in markets-PM  \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2006\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement, paragraphs 3-4, edits)  \par \par \uc2 ANKARA, May 24 (Reuters) - Turkey's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are in no hurry to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in financial markets, which have fallen sharply due to political and economic jitters, Prime Minister Tayyip Erdogan said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "We're not in a hurry to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets. Our \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not think such a thing and our government has no worries about it," Erdogan said in a televised speech.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which prizes its political independence, later issued a short statement making clear it was solely responsible for applying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 "As is known, we work with the government in determining the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy but applying the policy is directly the mandate and responsibility of our bank," it said.  \par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira <IYIX=> weakened to its lowest level against the dollar in two years on Wednesday, trading as far as 1.5630 against the dollar on the interbank market. It later rebounded slightly to trade at 1.5430 against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 In his speech, Erdogan stressed that other emerging markets were also experiencing market volatility and sought to play down the turbulence at home.  \par \par \uc2 Tera Stockbrokers managing director Emre Tezmen noted that Turkey, a candidate to join the European Union, had been significantly underperforming other markets.  \par \par \uc2 "Although the underperformance is normal (given) political risks, deteriorating inflation dynamics and existing economic fragilities caused by the widening current account deficit, the sell-off may have been excessive," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Erdogan rejected suggestions that his government was relaxing fiscal policy to shore up public support and ruled out calling early elections, despite widespread speculation about such a move which has contributed to market jitters.  \par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund (IMF), which completed a review mission to Turkey this week as part of a multi-billion dollar loan programme, has called for a cautious monetary policy and said additional government revenues should be saved.  \par \par \uc2 "The IMF comments were quite clear in that they called for fiscal adjustment which obviously is tough before the elections," said Claire Dissaux, emerging markets strategist at Calyon in Paris.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 TURKEY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|BNX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060524e25o000qd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
