\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish lira eases after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , shares firm  \b0\par\par\uc2 451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2006\par 17:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Feb 15 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira weakened against the dollar on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in response to lira strength.  \par \par \uc2 Bonds also weakened while shares firmed in what was generally a cautious mood ahead of the first testimony of the U.S. Federal Reserve's new chairman Ben Bernanke.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since November giving its usual explanation of "extreme volatility", but analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to spring back. Based on provisional data, the bank bought a record $4.6 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The lira closed at 1.3370 to the dollar on the interbank market, compared with 1.3271 on Tuesday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started at an asking price of 1.3272 lira to the dollar and went as high as 1.3420, firming again to 1.3310 in Thursday-dated trade.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling trend is continuing. (The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) provided an opportunity for foreigners to enter the market. With lira strengthening set to continue, there is expected to be more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said one banker.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on the benchmark Sept. 5, 2007 bond rose to 13.89 percent from 13.84 percent, but fell to 13.77 percent in Thursday-dated trade.  \par \par \uc2 The main Istanbul share index <.XU100> closed 0.68 percent higher at 43,803.98, recovering some of the 1.22 percent loss a day earlier. Trading volume rose slightly to 1.39 billion lira ($1.04 billion) from 1.38 billion a day earlier.  \par \par \uc2 "All global markets today were waiting for the statements from the Fed... Nobody wanted to change positions because of that," said Info Securities research director Mukrim Hatipoglu.  \par \par \uc2 After markets closed, Bernanke said the U.S. economy was running so close to capacity that it faced heightened risks of an outbreak in inflation that could require higher interest rates to tame.  \par \par \uc2 Among active shares, Akbank ended 1.74 percent higher at 11.7 lira after it said it had hired Swiss-based UBS as exclusive consultant to look for acquisition and other partnership possibilities.  \par \par \uc2 There was little reaction to a finance ministry official saying Turkey will not make concessions on a 15 percent withholding tax on financial instruments which it introduced at the start of this year despite demands from foreign investors.  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry had a meeting on Tuesday night with foreign bankers, bolstering hopes that it may show flexibility.  \par \par \uc2 Investors have stopped trading American Depositary Receipts, Global Depositary Receipts (GDR) and Depositary Receipts on the Istanbul Stock Exchange since the tax was introduced.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060215e22f001iu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
