\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to weaken lira  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gamze Alarslan  \par \uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2006\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote, releads)  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Feb 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since November to weaken the lira, but analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to spring back.  \par \par \uc2 Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some $4.6 billion, a record amount, calculated from provisional bank data.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started at an asking price of 1.3272 lira to the dollar and went as high as 1.3420, bankers who had sold to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 The lira closed at 1.3370 but firmed to 1.3310 in after hours trade. It closed last year at 1.35 to the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 "In recent days increases have been observed in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales affected by developments in international markets," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement said.  \par \par \uc2 "Therefore to prevent extreme volatility which has occurred and is expected to occur, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  today to buy (dollars for lira)," it added.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters, reeling from competition from China and other emerging economies, have been calling for a weaker lira while Turkey's current account deficit -- the main weak spot in a booming economy -- is widening.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were expected but the weakening these were likely to trigger would then draw fresh interest in lira assets from investors.  \par \par \uc2 "People have been waiting to get in ... You'll see a lot of interest in getting back in now," Deutsche Bank Strategist Jens Nystedt said.  \par \par \uc2 That will likely push the lira up again.  \par \par \uc2 TESTED AGAIN  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be tested again," Nystedt said.  \par \par \uc2 Last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  six times to buy dollars, mopping up $14.6 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The market had expected another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the Bank was seen as less likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  than last year because it has moved to formal inflation targeting and says inflation will more likely come in above the target than below it.  \par \par \uc2 Weakening the lira tends to boost inflation.  \par \par \uc2 CAIB economist Simon Quijano-Evans also said this was a good chance to move into Turkish debt.  \par \par \uc2 "We would expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  today, with similar amounts, and see these levels as a good opportunity to open positions in domestic debt, looking to the 2011 TRY bond, given the rise in compound yields to levels of 13.3 percent."  \par \par \uc2 Yields on the benchmark Sept. 5, 2007 bond rose to 13.91 percent on Wednesday from 13.84 percent on Tuesday. (Additional reporting by Emma Ross-Thomas)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 TURKEY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|MD|BNX|ABX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060215e22f000md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
