\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish markets firmer in quiet trade  \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2005\par 16:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Dec 28 (Reuters) - The fall of the U.S. dollar in international markets lifted the Turkish lira on Wednesday despite subdued interest in emerging market assets ahead of the new year holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The lira <IYIX=> firmed slightly to 1.3480 compared with the previous day's 1.3485 in line with the euro's gains against the greenback in global markets.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rose nearly one percent on the day to one-week highs against the dollar after surprisingly strong German consumer sentiment data. Turkish investors closely watch euro/dollar moves to take positions in lira.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on the benchmark June 27, 2007 bond fell to 13.80 percent from 13.86 percent on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The main Istanbul share index <.XU100> rose 0.52 percent to 39,220.17 points, hitting a fresh record close in thin volume.  \par \par \uc2 "Stocks were bought because of the tax advantage," said Alan Investment's Gulizar Ozdemir Turk.  \par \par \uc2 Turkey will introduce a 15 percent withholding tax on financial investment instruments such as shares and bonds on Jan. 1, 2006. This has encouraged investors to buy in the few days ahead of the introduction of the tax.  \par \par \uc2 In daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying auctions, aimed to strengthen Turkey's reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased a maximum $45 million at an average 1.3487 lira against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has bought $7.4 billion so far this year, excluding the purchases in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 TURKEY\b0 