\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Turkish c.bank buys dollars to stem lira gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Asli Kandemir  \par \uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2005\par 09:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with latest market data)  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying so far $2.6 billion for lira to counter the strength of the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bankers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 1537 GMT, best bids on the lira <IYIX=> stood at 1.3700 against the dollar on the interbank market, compared with 1.3550 before the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the sixth time this year.  \par \par \uc2 Under its floating exchange rate regime, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at times of excessive volatility.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in Friday's statement that foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales had increased in recent days because of global liquidity conditions.  \par \par \uc2 "The volatility in the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become more evident in line with the change in the U.S. dollar's value in international markets," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 Based on Friday's closing level, the lira has lost 2.06 percent of its value against the dollar this year.  \par \par \uc2 Positive global investment sentiment and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows into emerging markets have recently fuelled lira appreciation against a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made up of one dollar and 0.77 euro, bankers said.  \par \par \uc2 The informal basket which is tracked closely by bankers was at 2.58 lira before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , slightly above 2.56 lira when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 4.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was anticipated looking at the basket level. Banks may have been caught in short positions in the dollar," a banker said.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be more aggressive in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets on the back of a widening current account deficit and inflation targeting due to start on Jan. 1.  \par \par \uc2 "In light of the rapid deterioration in the current account balance, and prospects that it may not improve materially next year, there may be a case for more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the CBT in 2006 to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it aids a narrower deficit," 4CAST analyst Caroline Gorman said.  \par \par \uc2 The current account deficit jumped to $16.35 billion in the first nine months of 2005 from $10.62 billion in the same period last year, outstripping all original estimates.  \par \par \uc2 IMF, Turkey's main mentor on economic policies, said the deficit was likely to be around six percent of gross national product in 2005, and it may not decline much next year.  \par \par \uc2 Yet analysts did not foresee a major change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate regime next year when it would start inflation targeting.  \par \par \uc2 Next year's IMF-backed CPI target was set at five percent, down from this year's eight percent.  \par \par \uc2 "However, with the move to formal inflation targeting from January, we suspect the CBT will be wary about instigating any changes to its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy that might make its inflation targeting effort more difficult" Gorman said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought around $18 billion this year through direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and daily dollar purchasing auctions to strengthen its reserves.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $41.849 billion in the week ending Nov. 11.  \par \par \uc2 (Additonal reporting by Gamze Alarslan in Istanbul)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 TURKEY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|MD|ABN|M|D|BNX|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051118e1bi001cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
