\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Turkish inflation seen on track on seasonal factors  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gamze Alarslan  \par \uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2005\par 10:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, July 29 (Reuters) - Turkish producer prices should fall for a second consecutive month in July while seasonal factors will keep consumer prices down despite high oil prices, a Reuters poll showed on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 In a survey of 21 banks and brokerages, the median forecast rise in the consumer price index (CPI) month-on-month was 0.15 percent while the producer price index (PPI) was seen down 0.10 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The median forecast for private sector manufacturing prices was a rise of 0.50 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "I believe that any negative effect from energy prices will be limited due to positive seasonal conditions," said TEB Investment analyst Banu Kivci Tokali.  \par \par \uc2 At its monthly meeting in July the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its key borrowing and lending rates unchanged at 14.25 and 18.25 percent respectively for the first time this year, and said recent data suggested the downtrend in inflation could be slowing.  \par \par \uc2 The government's IMF-backed inflation target for 2005 is 8 percent, and the bank said next year's target of 5 percent was only achievable if domestic demand was kept under control.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most recent bi-weekly survey shows year-end consumer price inflation at 7.39 percent, lower than a previous forecast and the government target.  \par \par \uc2 "Appreciation of the lira will support declines in clothing and food price inflation," said Tokali.  \par \par \uc2 Hefty borrowing by local banks boosted Turkish lira liquidity and its position against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last two months, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week.  \par \par \uc2 In June, \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's consumer price index (CPI) rose 0.10 percent month-on-month for an annual rise of 8.95 percent, and the producer price index (PPI) fell 0.48 percent to produce a annual increase of 4.25 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The State Statistics Institute will publish the July inflation data on August 3.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -------  July (%)                   CPI       PPI\par         Ak Investment              0.42      0.28\par         Bender                    -0.20      0.80\par         Deniz Investment          -0.40      0.14\par         Disbank                    0.35      0.00\par         Dogus VDF                  0.10      0.10\par         EFG Istanbul               0.00      0.00\par         Finansbank                -0.10     -0.30\par         Garanti Bankasi            0.43      0.04\par         Garanti Investment         0.00      0.10\par         HSBC                      -0.30     -0.20\par         Is Bankasi                -0.20     -0.10\par         JP Morgan                  0.15     -0.24\par         Oyak Bank                  0.31     -0.04\par         Oyak Investment            0.00     -0.10\par         Raymond James              0.30      0.20\par         Sabanci Holding            0.20     -0.10\par         Sekerbank                  0.21     -0.16\par         TEB Investment             0.25     -0.22\par         TSKB                       0.15     -0.20\par         West LB                    0.20     -0.20\par         Yapi Kredi                 0.00     -0.20\par  -----------------------------------------------\par  Median                            0.15     -0.10\par  Mean                              0.09     -0.06\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 piz ECONOMY-TURKEY-INFLATION (POLL)|LAN