\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys dollars to cool lira  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Asli Kandemir  \par \uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2005\par 09:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds banker's volume estimate)  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, June 3 (Reuters) - Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for new lira in a strong wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday prompted by foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling in recent days amid strong demand for Turkish assets.  \par \par \uc2 One banker said the volume of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had exceeded $1 billion and appeared to be heading towards $1.5 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The lira closed at 1.3635 against the dollar on the interbank market <IYIX=>, compared with 1.3375 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The lira finished at 1.3475 against the dollar on Thursday, firming from a previous 1.3650.  \par \par \uc2 "As a result of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales in recent days, linked to the continued increase in positive expectations regarding our country's economy, excessive volatility was observed in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a written statement.  \par \par \uc2 Markets have shrugged off "no" votes in this week's French and Dutch referendums on the EU constitution, despite earlier fears that they could harm Turkey's bid to start European Union entry talks in October.  \par \par \uc2 "We see this as an opportunistic move to increase \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves while ... aiming at pre-empting any possible volatility lying ahead from political noise out of the EU," said Bank Austria Creditanstalt analyst Simon Quijano-Evans.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by $502 million to $35.773 billion in the week to May 27.  \par \par \uc2 The bank last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on March 9, buying dollars. Friday's action was the third time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We think that the recent increase in cash inflow has triggered the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, and we expect the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases to be high," said Oyak Securities Chief Economist Mehmet Besimoglu.  \par \par \uc2 Aside from Turkey's prospects for EU membership, investor interest in the country has been boosted by a strong economic recovery from a 2001 financial crisis, backed by multi-billion dollar loan deals with the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 Markets were also buoyed on Thursday by Turkey's sale of a $1.25 billion 15-year Eurobond which attracted strong demand. JP Morgan and Lehman Brothers were mandated for the issue.  \par \par \uc2 Investor attention is now focused on May inflation data, scheduled for release after the market closes on Friday, with another benign outcome expected to lead to further interest rate cuts. (Additional reporting by Humeyra Pamuk)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 TURKEY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|BNX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050603e163000ge\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\