\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fed drags market down, lira worst hit.  \b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 23 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira led high-yield emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down on Wednesday, after a hawkish message from the Federal Reserve stoked expectations of bigger U.S. interest rate rises.   \par \par \uc2  In a widely expected move, the Federal Open Market Committee nudged rates higher by a quarter percentage point to 2.75 percent, its 7th rate rise since June.   \par \par \uc2  The committee, however, said "pressures on inflation have picked up" and the risks for growth and price stability would only remain balanced with appropriate policy action.   \par \par \uc2  "This was overall negative for emerging markets. A lot of capital has been sucked out," said a senior trader at a UK bank. "The market did not react to the statement yesterday because it was too late, but it was really hit this morning."   \par \par \uc2  The prospect of faster U.S. rate hikes unnerves emerging market investors because they would erode the relative attractiveness of high yield assets.   \par \par \uc2  The lira fell to a two-month low against the dollar, on the interbank market , trading at 1.3630 by 1025 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  Tolga Ediz, director of emerging markets research at Lehman Brothers, said part of the lira's woes stem from Turkey's dependence on foreign investors to finance its current account deficit. "When you are essentially dependent on international liquidity, once there is a change in external environment ... you get hit. And at this point there is still a risk of further decline," he said.   \par \par \uc2  Another factor, he said, was the delay in sealing a $10 billion loan deal with the International Monetary Fund which is tied to key social security, tax and pension reforms.   \par \par \uc2  Adding momentum to lira losses was Turkish Economy Minister Ali Babacan's comment on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market even if there is a rapid capital outflow.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on March 9 and purchased as much as $2.5 billion as the lira hit four-year highs against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Babacan also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would purchase between $9 billion and $10 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.   \par \par \uc2  SLOVAK CROWN SLUMPS   \par \par \uc2  Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also down across the board, with the Slovak crown the worst hit. It dropped over 1/2 a percent against the euro  to its lowest levels in nearly 4 months at 39.26, though it later recovered some lost ground.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts continue to see the most vulnerable \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as those where major long positions have been built up. The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of them, having hit a string of record highs this year.   \par \par \uc2  "People are not ready to call a bottom on this move yet. They are trying to close down positions where they can, you can see that in the Slovak crown, which is one of the big underperformers today," said Koon Chow, emerging markets strategist at CSFB.   \par \par \uc2  Chow said he remained positive on the outlook for the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the medium-term, but would not look to get back in yet. "I want to see these markets stabilise first before re-entering, but the signs are there. Euro/zloty is not making new highs today."   \par \par \uc2  The zloty was down around 0.4 percent against the euro at 4.12 .   \par \par \uc2  Polish asset markets are finding some support from growing expectations for an interest rate cut from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at next week's policy meeting.   \par \par \uc2  News on Wednesday of a weaker-than-forecast 2.4 percent annual rise in February retail sales further bolstered the case for reducing key rates from 6.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050323e13n0089a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
