\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Lira hits new peaks, rand dips from highs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2005\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 15 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira hit its best levels in over nine months on Tuesday with appetite seen returning for high-yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though the South African rand lagged, in part on softer than forecast growth data.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's slide to 10-day lows against the euro on Monday continued to lend a bullish backdrop to high yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Turkish lira one of the main beneficiaries.  \par \par \uc2 Domestic factors are also leaning in the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's favour with an auction of new five-year lira paper on Tuesday seen attracting good foreign demand.  \par \par \uc2 "Investor appetite for high yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be increasing again. We've seen that in the price action in the Brazilian real overnight," said Koon Chow, emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at CSFB.  \par \par \uc2 The real firmed one percent to 2.579 per dollar in domestic trade on Monday , its strongest since June 2002.  \par \par \uc2 By 1050 GMT, the lira traded at 1.31 to the dollar on the interbank market , up from 1.3150 at Monday's close.  \par \par \uc2 "On the Turkish side, there are three good factors arguing for the downside (in dollar/lira)," said Chow.  \par \par \uc2 Firstly, increased confidence in the lira after its redenomination on Jan. 1 continues to see locals switch foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits back into lira.  \par \par \uc2 Secondly, portfolio inflows, likely to be reflected in Tuesday's bond auction and, finally, inflows associated with the hedging of lira-denominated bonds issued by non-Turkish entities.  \par \par \uc2 "We've seen around 1.8 billion lira ($1.4 billion) worth of issuance in just over a month, which is a huge amount.  \par \par \uc2 "These non-Turkish issuers don't have lira cashflow so ultimately they will have to buy lira some way to pay the coupon."  \par \par \uc2 Investors have been scrambling to gain exposure to lira assets ever since the European Union granted Turkey a date to start entry talks in October.  \par \par \uc2 Chow added a note of caution on the bullish outlook, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be wary of allowing the lira to rise too far, hurting \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the next 24 hours, though it will probably only offer better levels to go long (lira)."  \par \par \uc2 RAND DIPS  \par \par \uc2 South Africa's rand paused for breath after four strong rising sessions, with slightly softer than expected fourth quarter GDP growth giving investors an excuse to trim long positions.  \par \par \uc2 The South African economy grew four percent in the fourth quarter, down from a strong 5.7 percent rate in the third quarter, leaving full year growth at 3.7 percent  \par \par \uc2 The rand traded was down 0.64 percent at 6.04 to the dollar .  \par \par \uc2 Expectations of an uptick in Polish inflation in January consumer price data due at 1500 GMT helped the zloty firm back under the four-per-euro mark .  \par \par \uc2 January CPI is forecast to rise to an annual rate of 4.6 percent, from 4.4 percent in December, adding to the case that interest rates have bottomed out at 6.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Claire Dissaux at Calyon said the data "will be a reminder that inflation is likely to spike this quarter well above the 2.5 percent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  target, playing for a freeze in interest rates that keeps carry attraction high in the near term."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty traded at 3.9883 to the euro  from 4.0012 and at 3.0725 to\par the dollar        from 3.0848. The Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par try and curb the rising leu, buying around 50-60 million euros\par according to traders.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank stepped in after speculative buying drove the leu up sharply to two-year highs against the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday. The leu traded at 36,450 per euro , down over four percent from its highs following the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050215e12f008vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
