\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Turkey acts to curb lira, new high for Slovak crown.  \b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2005\par 12:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 27 (Reuters) - Further strengthening in emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  and raised the prospect of similar action in Slovakia on Thursday, while the Czech crown calmed ahead of an interest rate decision.  \par \par \uc2 The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought dollars for lira to curb exchange rate volatility, in its first market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since February 2004.  \par \par \uc2 The new lira has risen to near 10 month highs following the European Union's decision in late December to allow Turkey to start entry talks in October, raising expectations of a surge in foreign investment inflows.  \par \par \uc2 By 1041 GMT, the new lira was at 1.3440 per dollar in interbank trade , down from pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highs around 1.3215. Turkish banking sources said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought around 150-200 million dollars on the market.  \par \par \uc2 "It's probably a combination of the size of flows coming into the bond market and the extent of the lira move that has triggered the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Lucy Bethell, emerging markets analyst at RBS Financial Markets.  \par \par \uc2 "People had been getting increasingly short (of dollars), but the question now is whether they'll take it as cue to book profits, or an opportunity for better entry levels.  \par \par \uc2 "Sentiment is so strong on Turkey at the moment that at some point I'd expect people to get back in."  \par \par \uc2 Foreign trade minister Kursad Tuzmen said he hoped the lira would fall to 1.5-1.6 per dollar. Its strength has contributed to large trade and current account deficits.  \par \par \uc2 NEW HIGHS FOR SLOVAK CROWN  \par \par \uc2 Dealers are also on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  red alert in Slovakia after investors' ongoing enthusiasm for the country pushed the crown to an all-time high against the euro on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The crown was flat percent at 38.44 per euro, having briefly touched a fresh high earlier at 38.376 .  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried to stem the crown's rise since mid-2003, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the last month to keep the unit above 38.50 per euro, but said it had no comment on the latest move.  \par \par \uc2 The bank could cut rates at its monthly interest rate meeting on Friday, though further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen as more likely given the crown has grown increasingly immune to rate cuts following a 200 basis point loosening to 4.0 percent last year.  \par \par \uc2 Even that is unlikely to reverse the crown's uptrend.  \par \par \uc2 "If you believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  most people would believe that any setback in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be rather small and temporary," Barclays Capital emerging markets analyst Jeff Gable said. The Czech crown dipped from Wednesday's 28-month highs to trade around 30.12 per euro ahead of an interest rate decision.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to hold rates steady at 2.5 percent and market watchers will focus on any comments about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength arising from an afternoon monetary policy news conference.  \par \par \uc2 The crown has risen almost 10 percent in the past 12 months, most recently boosted by speculation about the sale of state-owned phone group Cesky Telekom (SPTTsp.PR) for an estimated $3 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Further evidence of a benign inflation environment in South Africa came from December producer price numbers, with the annual rate well below expectations at 1.9 percent, down from 2.5 percent in November.  \par \par \uc2 The news had little impact on the rand, which found good support from the buoyant tone across emerging markets. It traded virtually flat around 5.93 per dollar .  \par \par \uc2 The Romanian leu eased about three quarters of a percent against the euro, weighed by Prime Minister Calin Tariceanu's comment there might be a delay to plans to allow foreigners access to leu deposits from April, following talks with the IMF.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the Fund might call for a delay due to the risk the move triggers a wave of speculative capital, complicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's task of curbing inflation.  \par \par \uc2 The leu was down 0.73 percent at 28,938 per euro .   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050127e11r009yf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
