 effect of lower returns on long lira positions.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK CROWN STEADIES AFTER \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday after the crown surged to record highs against the euro around 38.5 , triggering a move to 38.74 initially, before the crown recovered some ground. The rate stabilised around 38.70 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 A bigger than expected November trade gap was seen preventing a further recovery in the crown, with the deficit widening to 3.953 billion crowns ($134.5 million), above a market consensus forecast of 2.7 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Even so, most analysts continue to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fighting an unstoppable strengthening trend in the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , driven by strong foreign investment inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Carlos Teixeira, analyst at Goldman Sachs, said the Slovaks' latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was no surprise.  \par \par \uc2 "Their action may stem appreciation temporarily, as last happened in December, but we expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resume its strengthening," Teixeira said in a research note. "This will help the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meet its inflation target and leaves the door open to further rate cuts."  \par \par \uc2 The crown traded at 38.69 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar peeled back more of last week's strong gains against the euro , lending a broadly firmer tone to high yield emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The South African rand was again the best performer, rising 0.82 percent against the dollar to trade around 5.94 .   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050111e11b00cch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
