\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Debt-Turkish debt gains as market turns positive.   \b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2004\par 12:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 11 (Reuters) - Emerging market debt bounced to erase some of the previous sessions' losses on Tuesday, with \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking centre stage after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy lira, a move traders said calmed the market.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is higher, although we will see if bonds will hold when New York comes in. Now it seems 'yes' - we have seen some buyers," said a bond trader in London.   \par \par \uc2 By 1031 GMT, the risk premium for emerging market debt over U.S. Treasuries had narrowed by 13 basis points to 556 basis points on the benchmark JPMorgan Emerging Market Bond Index Plus , its first positive move after a three-day sell-off.   \par \par \uc2 Investors dumped emerging market debt late last week and on Monday on rising worries U.S. interest rates would rise sooner than expected.   \par \par \uc2 Higher rates in safe-haven U.S. Treasury notes would make them more attractive, and prompt a flee of investors from riskier emerging market assets.   \par \par \uc2 "The market couldn't sustain this degree of selling, there was bound to be a bounce-back. But what was going on in 2002 and throughout 2003 with extremely low U.S. and European rates...that story is probably over now," said Charles Robertson, EMEA economist at ING Barings. The risk premium of Turkey's portion of the EMBI+ tightened 37 basis points to 513 basis points.   \par \par \uc2 Turkey's benchmark 2034 dollar bond recovered from Monday's steep losses to rise two points to 84.5 percent of face value.   \par \par \uc2 "My feeling is that it is still probably oversold, but probably the wider market is also oversold. People are still in pain after the past week," said Timothy Ash, analyst at Bear Stearns.   \par \par \uc2 Robertson said Turkey's external debt yields had become too expensive after a plethora of positive news and a global hunt for yield among investors in the past six to twelve months.   \par \par \uc2 "The sell-off in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt has meant a return to more sensible and sustainable levels," Robertson said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  BOOST   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market earlier on Tuesday, buying lira for U.S. dollars after a sharp weakening in the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  driven by political and emerging market worries.   \par \par \uc2 "I'm not sure they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily, it was probably more a case of dipping their toe in the water and seeing how it goes... but there were no bids in the market so it got quite a big (positive) reaction," said one London trader.   \par \par \uc2 The bank was reported to have stepped in around 1,565,000 per dollar , helping the lira recover to around 1,535,000.   \par \par \uc2 Turkish markets have been hammered in recent sessions by broad-based interest rate fears and also on concerns over a row between the government and powerful military on higher education reform.   \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Tayyip Erdogan unnerved markets last week when he said the government would talk to the IMF about lowering the primary surplus target.   \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday Erdogan helped calm the markets by saying the government was determined to maintain fiscal discipline and would keep its primary surplus high to help pay down public sector debt.   \par \par \uc2 Erdogan, addressing members of his ruling Justice and Development Party in parliament, said relations with the IMF would continue beyond the end of the current $19 billion loan deal next February in order to preserve confidence.   \par \par \uc2 He did not specify what kind of relations.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040511e05b0018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
