\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Turkish c. bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support ailing lira.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daren Butler   \par \uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2004\par 15:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, May 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying lira for dollars to underpin the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a sharp weakening fuelled by domestic and emerging market worries.   \par \par \uc2 The small-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - only the second time the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars since \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to a floating rate regime in 2001 - triggered a lira rebound from 12-month lows against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said it showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not allow excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially stepped into the market when the lira was around 1,565,000 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the morning, pushing it back to 1,530,000, bankers said.   \par \par \uc2 It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again after the official close at a level of 1,553,000 during Wednesday value-dated trade, prompting it to firm to 1,536,000 on the interbank market .   \par \par \uc2 The volume of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounted to some $30 million, bankers said.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market today, selling (dollars) as a result of excessive volatility," the bank said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 It said the volatility resulted from a narrowing of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity. It also lowered rates on its weekly foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lending to banks to six percent from 10 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Ozgur Altug, chief economist at brokerage Raymond James, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not allow excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 "We believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at the right time. The upward correction in the lira-dollar rate could continue but at a decelerated pace," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "The rising volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market started to disturb the bond market and consequently the debt dynamics, plus it was having an adverse impact on pricing behaviour in the manufacturing sector," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  previously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy lira in December 2002 around a level of 1,700,000 against the dollar. It has also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on eight occasions to buy dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Turkish markets have been hit in recent sessions by emerging market worries about a possible U.S. interest rate hike, a row between the government and the powerful military on higher education reform, and a widening current account deficit.   \par \par \uc2 There has also been concern that Turkey may veer away from IMF-backed targets. But Prime Minister Tayyip Erdogan said on Tuesday that a key measure of the government's IMF accord, the primary surplus, would be kept high in line with Fund wishes.   \par \par \uc2 Last week Erdogan unnerved markets by saying Ankara would talk to the IMF about lowering the primary surplus target.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sureyya Serdengecti had tried to soothe rattled markets on Monday, calling on the government to curb inflation risks and stick to a key primary surplus target under the country's $19 billion IMF loan accord.   \par \par \uc2 Serdengecti blamed banks' short trading positions for intensifying pressure on the lira.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040511e05b000sf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
