\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Turkish lira slips in early trade after bombs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2003\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Nov 21 (Reuters) - Turkey's lira slipped to best bids of 1,488,000 to the dollar in early trade on Friday after twin bomb attacks in Istanbul killed at least 27 and injured hundreds.  \par \par \uc2 The lira had fallen to close at 1,478,000 to the dollar on Thursday in thin trade following the suspected suicide attacks, which raised worries over investor confidence in the IMF debtor recovering from a financial crisis that peaked in February 2001.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it reserved the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy lira if the free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes under sustained selling pressure due to the bombings.  \par \par \uc2 Britain has warned Turkey may be the target of more terror attacks. Thursday's attacks hit the British consulate in Istanbul and the offices of London-based banking giant HSBC (HSBA.L) (HBC.N) in the city's financial district.  \par \par \uc2 Trade in Turkey's hefty domestic debt was set to begin around 0730 GMT. The busiest December 15, 2004 paper closed Thursday at yields of 29.07 percent, weaker than Wednesday's 28.69.  \par \par \uc2 The main stock index dived 7.37 percent to 14,617.53 points shortly after the attacks, prompting the Istanbul Stock Exchange (IMKB) to halt trading.  \par \par \uc2 Turkey's bourse will remain closed until December 1, when a one-week holiday to mark the end of the Muslim month of fasting concludes.  \par \par \uc2 The volatile lira has been rallying for much of 2003 as the economy showed signs of a full recovery from the financial crisis, helped by $16 billion in IMF lending.  \par \par \uc2 The lira and debt markets are due to close on Monday afternoon for the religious holiday and to reopen Friday of the same week.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031121dzbl001oy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
