\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Turkish lira off year highs after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 17:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Sept 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market pushed the lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from year highs, but equities and debt rose as investors remained upbeat about the country's economic recovery.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly stepped in to buy dollars for lira as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit levels of around 1,350,000 to the dollar from Wednesday's close of 1,353,000. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished the day at 1,374,000 on the interbank market .   \par \par \uc2 Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased more than $1 billion in its sixth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May.   \par \par \uc2 The lira's rally from record lows of around 1,750,000 in March threatens Turkish exports, the engine behind economic growth after a deep recession in 2001, and a year-end target of $7.4 billion for the current account deficit.   \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to dampen appetite for high-yielding Turkish debt. Benchmark August 18, 2004, bonds finished at 34.27 percent from Wednesday's 34.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "(The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is likely to prove to be ineffective - interest rates have fallen sharply, but they still provide an attractive backdrop and the new U.S. loan package has also been supportive," said Mehmet Simsek, emerging markets strategist at Merrill Lynch in London.   \par \par \uc2 Turkey this week inked an $8.5 billion loan deal with the United States that should boost debt-ridden Turkey's coffers and ease the treasury's domestic and foreign debt burden. Domestic debt alone stands at around $130 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Offers at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily auction to buy dollars on Thursday hit $249 million against a maximum sale of $75 million.   \par \par \uc2 The auctions and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have boosted its hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to record levels. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were at an all-time high of $31.468 billion on September 19.   \par \par \uc2 Shares on the Istanbul bourse's main index closed one percent higher at 13,935.67 points.   \par \par \uc2 "Buying is coming as the index reaches support levels. The positive atmosphere is still continuing and because the market is strong, buying has quite an effect," said Utku Yarpuzlu of Vakif Investment.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030925dz9p002c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
