\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging debt- \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  debt shrugs off  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 12:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - Turkish debt shrugged off a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that might have weakened international bond prices in London on Thursday, as investors still expect rates to fall boosting debt valuations. London traders estimated that Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought between $350 million and $650 million from banks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed the purchase, but did not give the amount.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A weaker lira could make domestic interest rates less likely to fall,\par as the lira, which has strengthened 21.5 percent this year, has played\par a big part in checking inflation. Prolonged high lira rate makes\par Turkish bonds as a whole less attractive, because domestic bond buyers\par would have less money to spend. But markets were unfazed. "There was a\par very muted reaction, the bonds got hit a bit and the bids came back,"\par said a trader at a U.S. bank in London. "But we are still expecting a\par 300 basis point rate cut next month." Turkey's benchmark 2030 dollar\par bond  was unchanged at 116.375 percent of face value. The country's\par shorter maturity benchmark the $1.5 billion 2010 bond              rose\par 0.375 points in price at 114.250.\par The country's segment  of the industry benchmark, JPMorgan's Emerging\par Market Bond Index plus        , fell in yield premium by two basis\par points compared with Treasuries.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The EMBI+ as a whole was unchanged at 486 basis points over Treasuries. "The lira will weaken a little bit and then it will strengthen again," said Peter Botoucharov, emerging markets economist at Commerzbank in London. "In Turkey we have a positive sentiment. It has entered a virtuous cycle where lower interest rates and falling rates have a positive impact on the fiscal accounts."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey has been generating rising primary surpluses in recent months, which makes the country's bonds ever more secure assets to hold. Turkey's economy has begun to consolidate a recovery from 2001's 9.4 percent economic contraction, the largest such recession in 50 years.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The country is implementing a programme backed with $16 billion in International Monetary Fund assistance after a shaky start. The AK Party, which took power following a landslide election victory in November last year, took six months to agree terms with the IMF. But investor confidence has been rising since the programme was agreed and the U.S.-led war in neighbouring Iraq proved shorter than expected. This week, Turkey signed an $8.5 billion loan deal with the United States, further boosting confidence.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA ALSO RISES  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russian debt nudged lower in yield as Wednesday's moves in Treasuries lifted prices, and on trader talk that the country might soon have it ratings upgraded.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury rose more than 0.6 percent in New York on Wednesday, although in London the bond fell slightly, by around 0.1 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In Russia there is very good demand thanks to rumours that Russia could be upped by two notches to investment grade by October," said the trader.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service placed Russia on upgrade watch at the end of July. It rates the country's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  obligations Ba2, at the upper end of the speculative grade rating range. A move to investment grade Baa3 would open Russia up to a much broader range of investors.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank's Botoucharov said he thought such a dramatic ratings move unlikely.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia's benchmark 2030 dollar bond rose 0.875 to 94.625 percent of face value.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030925dz9p001ie\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
