\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys dollars for lira.   \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2003\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Sept 10 (Reuters) - Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had bought dollars for lira on Wednesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began buying dollars at around 1,371,000 lira after it dipped to 1,370,000. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at around 1,389,000 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "A direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase (dollars) was made in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market today to prevent extreme fluctuations," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 The lira has surged in recent months amid upbeat sentiment about an economic recovery after the Turkish unit reached record lows of around 1,750,000 in March on worries the U.S-led war in Iraq would undermine \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on July 18, when it stepped in repeatedly as the lira reached levels around 1,375,000 to the dollar. The bank purchased $938 million that day.   \par \par \uc2 The lira has appreciated by more than 17 percent since the start of the year, raising concerns for Turkey's current account deficit which widened to $4 billion in the first half of the year against a revised year-end target of $7.4 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The lira's strength could also affect economic growth if exports become too expensive, hitting the manufacturing sector.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030910dz9a0021f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
