\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 3-Turk c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to arrest galloping lira. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Gamze Alarslan \par \uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2003\par 16:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, July 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for lira on Friday in the most intense wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since crisis ripped through \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial markets in early 2001, sending the lira into freefall. \par \par \uc2  This time the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb a rise in the lira as it reached 14-month highs of around 1,370,000 to the dollar, a rally the government fears could undermine exports. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had stepped in to arrest "lira volatility" but investors suspected the bank was more concerned about the impact of the strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the current account deficit, already gaping beyond targets. \par \par \uc2  The lira, traded freely since the financial crisis struck, later weakened to 1,403,000 after what traders said was a whole series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the bank during Friday trading. \par \par \uc2  "I think the only way this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be justified is for the level of the lira, not the volatility, despite what the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says," said Tolga Ediz, director in global economics at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  The lira has risen more than 20 percent against the dollar from record lows of around 1,750,000 in March amid fears over the economic impact of war in Iraq on Turkey's economy. \par \par \uc2  The current account deficit has widened to $3.47 billion in the first five months of the year against a year-end target of $6.1 billion under a $16 billion pact with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  Several bankers estimated Friday's total dollar purchases amounted to around $700 million, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not say how many dollars it bought. \par \par \uc2  DEMAND FOR DEBT DOMINATES \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  today made a direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent extreme volatility in the exchange rate," the bank said in a written statement released after its initial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The bank may need to act again as lira purchases continue on confidence Turkey's frail economy is recovering. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said foreign demand for high-yielding local debt was the main driver behind the lira's rise as Turkey works to service some $125 billion in domestic debt. \par \par \uc2  Appetite for the lira was reflected in a daily dollar purchase auction on Friday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  met $50 million of the $214 million offered by investors. \par \par \uc2  "Yields have brought in portfolio flows from abroad...It (the lira's rally) is being principally driven by this ongoing refinancing of domestic debt," said Philip Poole, senior emerging markets analyst at ING Barings in London. \par \par \uc2  The busiest August 18, 2004, debt traded at yields of 46.78 percent on the secondary market on Friday compared to a yearly consumer price inflation target of 20 percent for 2003, a wide profit margin for investors. \par \par \uc2  The bank is bolstering its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves through its purchase auctions of dollars that some analysts say should be raised to $80 million to $90 million daily if the bank is to succeed in arresting the lira. \par \par \uc2  The bank has yet to confirm it stepped in repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the day. It last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars on June 9 when the lira posted a previous 12-month high at 1,409,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Despite its recent rally, the lira has fallen some 50 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it was floated in 2001. \par \par \uc2  - Additional reporting by Mark Bentley. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030718dz7i00fa6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
