\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Turkey - May 23. \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2003\par 08:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, May 23 (Reuters) - These are the leading stories in the Turkish press on Friday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  HURRIYET \par \par \uc2  - Turkey's parliament passes a landmark law late on Thursday bolstering workers' rights. \par \par \uc2  - Economy Minister Ali Babacan says key IMF-backed legislation could be delayed because the government cannot ignore other laws already before parliament. \par \par \uc2  - Turkey's finance minister expects no hitches with a latest IMF review of Turkey's $16 billion pact. Turkey has done most of its homework, he says. \par \par \uc2  SABAH \par \par \uc2  - Turkey cuts value added tax (VAT) on fruit and vegetable seeds, some yoghurts and baby food. \par \par \uc2  - Is Bank general manager Ersin Ozince says unregistered capital dominates the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to arrest a lira rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  - Parliament is set to pass EU-inspired laws allowing Kurdish language broadcasting on privately-owned TV channels. The powers of State Security Courts (DGMs) will be curtailed, the military will no longer sit on a board licencing films and music, and foreign officials can observe elections. \par \par \uc2  CUMHURIYET \par \par \uc2  - Turkey's army chief Hilmi Ozkok tells the prime minister more radical elements of his Justice and Development Party (AKP) are taking courage from the latest EU reform package, some articles of which are making the military uncomfortable. \par \par \uc2  MILLIYET \par \par \uc2  - Iraqi oil will soon begin to flow through a pipeline to Turkey after the U.N. lifts trade sanctions on Baghdad. \par \par \uc2  RADIKAL \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $450 million in a Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest a rise in the lira's value against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - The government has abandoned plans to cancel an anti-terror law, previously part of its latest EU reform drive. \par \par \uc2  DUNYA \par \par \uc2  - Consumer lending has risen 22 percent in the first five months of the year, a sign of growth in Turkey's frail economy. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030523dz5n00dgz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
