\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish markets seen steady on c.bank action, IMF. \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2003\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, May 22 (Reuters) - Turkish markets were expected to hold steady on Thursday after a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars and as the International Monetary Fund began a critical review of Turkey's $16 billion pact. \par \par \uc2  The lira  closed on Wednesday at 1,489,000 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in at levels around 1,452,000. It was trading at 1,484,000 early on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The lira has rallied to levels not seen since last June with the swift end of the war in neighbouring Iraq, worrying exporters and other businesses an over-valued lira could threaten \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cheered stockbrokers, and the main index  climbed 1.09 percent to 10,540.85 points after weeks of losses or limited gains that many traders have blamed on the strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave the market a boost in dollar terms," said Emre Balkeser, sales trader at Alfa Securities. "The market shouldn't go below 10,500 today." \par \par \uc2  Balkeser said investors were also pleased with successful Treasury auctions this week and were still expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut key interest rates on signs inflation is falling. \par \par \uc2  Speculation of a rate cut helped debt yields firm, and March 26, 2004, papers finished on Wednesday at 52.12 percent from a previous 53.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Investors are eyeing the IMF review amid worries the government has dragged its feet on reforms it promised the fund for a latest loan tranche of $500 million. \par \par \uc2  The last review of the pact was delayed for months by a general election, little action on reforms and a lack of agreement on IMF demands for a cost-cutting 2003 budget. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030522dz5m00dls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
