\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Turkish c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to curb lira moves. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Gamze Alarslan \par \uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2003\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, May 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy dollars for lira on Wednesday afternoon to stem a rise in the lira's value that some investors say poses a threat to exports and the current account. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as an IMF team arrived in Ankara for the Fund's latest review of Turkey's economic pact. Analysts said potential problems with completing the review may help weaken the lira in the coming weeks and narrow the current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  Bankers told Reuters the bank had stepped in as the lira traded at around 1,452,000 to the dollar. It closed at bids of 1,489,000 on the interbank market . \par \par \uc2  The lira, which closed Tuesday at 1,460,000, has soared around 19 percent from record lows of some 1,772,000 to the dollar seen in March, when investors worried war in Iraq and tensions with the United States might send the country back into recession. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  today \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the buying side on seeing a repeat of extreme volatility," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  The bank last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on May 12 to buy dollars for lira. It had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy lira for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on December 24, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 1,700,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The strong lira has sparked complaints from exporters and other business groups who see a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as helping their export competitiveness in terms of price. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will most likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to arrest any future firming of the lira, floated amid a February 2001 financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  IMF TENSIONS MAY SPARK LIRA SALES \par \par \uc2  While seeing no sharp fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming weeks, analysts said the government's foot-dragging on a swathe of IMF-backed reforms, including measures on public spending and taxation, may weaken the lira if problems arise with a visiting IMF review team. \par \par \uc2  "I think the IMF review might provide some help in preventing the appreciation of the lira...I'm not surprised the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the lira in real terms is very strong," said Marco Annunziata at Deutsche Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "It makes you somewhat concerned looking at the current account prospects going forward." \par \par \uc2  The IMF is due to complete its review of Turkey's $16 billion pact within two weeks. Its board could meet in early June to approve a $500 million loan tranche provided it is satisfied Ankara has met the pact's conditions. \par \par \uc2  Turkey's foreign trade deficit jumped 74.6 percent in the first quarter of the year to $4.08 billion, raising worries for the current account. \par \par \uc2  The current account deficit had jumped to $1.18 billion in the first two months of the year, the latest available data, against a deficit of $286 million in the same period of 2002. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the lira's strength did not reflect economic fundamentals but was linked to widespread sales of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks to meet corporate tax payments in lira. \par \par \uc2  "The extreme volatility does not stem from the balance of payments or reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  substitution, it is thought to be the result of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales for heavy tax payments...and the delaying of demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it said. \par \par \uc2  The lira is now around 54 percent below the level it was at just before the 2001 financial crisis struck. \par \par \uc2  - Additional reporting by Mark Bentley in Istanbul. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030521dz5l00pmv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
