\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Turk lira ends slightly down after CB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ayla Jean Yackley \par \uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2003\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Adds close, quote, bond tap, alters dateline to Ankara from Istanbul) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA, May 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday to buy dollars hardly dampened the appetite for lira as upbeat traders saw little incentive to part with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lira  finished at 1,501,000 to the dollar, down slightly from Friday's 1,498,000, but was trading at that level in Tuesday-dated trade. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed to around 1,486,000 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, traders said. \par \par \uc2  These levels have not been seen since June 2002 and come with the relief of a swift end to the war in neighbour Iraq and signs the Turkey is committed to a $16 billion IMF pact. \par \par \uc2  Shares and debt both edged higher. \par \par \uc2  It was the only the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars. The first came on December 2 when the lira had rallied to around 1,510,000. \par \par \uc2  The bank said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the lira against excessive fluctuations in value and was not uncomfortable with the lira's levels against the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  But some traders saw it as an effort to protect exports, a main source of growth for Turkey's frail economy, and came amid fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was over-valued. \par \par \uc2  "Every one of us was getting concerned about the value of the lira. Although (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) says the level of the lira was not the main reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...I think the bank is not happy with a level below 1,500,000 now," said Yarkin Cebeci at JPMorgan. \par \par \uc2  Turkey's year-on-year foreign trade deficit jumped 74.6 percent in the first quarter of the year to $4.08 billion. \par \par \uc2  TURKEY ISSUES DEBT \par \par \uc2  The Treasury said on Monday it would increase its 2013 dollar bond  via Morgan Stanley and JPMorgan, capitalising on strong investor demand for high yielding debt. \par \par \uc2  Traders have been expecting the tap as Turkey's debt yields fall to more acceptable levels for borrowing. \par \par \uc2  Closely-watched May 26, 2004, debt firmed to yields of 50.68 percent from Friday's 51.19 percent on the secondary market. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury on Monday successfully sold 1,536 trillion lira (around $1 billion) worth of three-month papers at a lower-than-expected maximum yield of 41.96 percent. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said in a Reuters poll ahead of the auction they saw the rate at an average 42.6 percent. \par \par \uc2  Some investors believe a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cut is imminent amid signs consumer price inflation was falling towards an IMF-backed year-end target of 20 percent. \par \par \uc2  Others say the bank may wait until after a latest IMF review of Turkey's $16 billion pact, due to begin on May 21. \par \par \uc2  Equities were little moved by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the main index  edging up 0.68 percent in the first session to 10,712.87 points. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030512dz5c00t18\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
