\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish lira little changed after CB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2003\par 12:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, May 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday to buy dollars hardly dampened the appetite for lira as upbeat traders saw little incentive to part with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lira was trading at 1,497,000 to the dollar on the interbank market by mid-day, down slightly from 1,492,000 in earlier trade just before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished on Friday at 1,498,000. \par \par \uc2  These levels have not been seen since June 2002 and come with the relief of a swift end to the war in neighbour Iraq and signs the Turkish government is committed to a $16 billion IMF pact. \par \par \uc2  The bank said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the lira against excessive fluctuations in value and was not uncomfortable with the lira's levels against the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  But some traders saw it as an effort to protect exports, a main source of growth for Turkey's frail economy. \par \par \uc2  "It was a positive move. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems worried the lira's (rise) may create imbalances. The current account numbers show that is a threat," said Hakan Avci at Global Securities. \par \par \uc2  Turkey's year-on-year foreign trade deficit jumped 74.6 percent in the first quarter of the year to $4.08 billion. \par \par \uc2  Equities were little moved by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the main index edging up 0.22 percent in the first session to 10,664.34 points. \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate and the lack of an exciting story spell a flat stock market," Avci said, pointing out there was no expectation at this time for dollar demand in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury on Monday sold 1,536 trillion lira (around $1 billion) worth of three-month papers at a lower-than-expected maximum yield of 41.96 percent. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said in a Reuters poll ahead of the auction they saw the rate at an average 42.6 percent. \par \par \uc2  Closely-watched May 26, 2004, debt firmed to yields of 50.74 percent from Friday's 51.19 percent on the secondary market. \par \par \uc2  Some investors believe a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cut is imminent amid signs consumer price inflation was falling towards an IMF-backed year-end target of 20 percent. \par \par \uc2  Others say the bank may wait until after a latest IMF review of Turkey's $16 billion pact, due to begin on May 21. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030512dz5c00k2o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
